---
import "../styles/global.css";
import { SITE_BASE } from "../features/auth/auth-client";

const homeHref = `${SITE_BASE}/`;
const contactEmail = "2401117078@student.buksu.edu.ph";
const updated = "28 September 2026";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        try {
          let t = localStorage.getItem("ccna-theme");
          if (t !== "dark" && t !== "light") t = "light";
          document.documentElement.dataset.theme = t;
        } catch {
          document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "light";
        }
      })();
    </script>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${SITE_BASE}/favicon.svg`} />
    <title>Privacy policy — CCNA 2 v7 Practice Exams</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="What the CCNA 2 v7 Practice Exams site collects when you sign in with a Buksu Google account, and your rights under the Data Privacy Act of 2012."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="policy">
      <span class="policy-kicker">CCNA 2 v7 — SRWE Practice Exams</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This is a student practice site for the CCNA 2 v7 (SRWE) course. To keep the
        practice exams limited to enrolled students, it uses <strong>Sign in with
        Google</strong> and stores a small record of who has signed in. This page
        explains exactly what is collected and why, in line with the <strong>Data
        Privacy Act of 2012 (RA 10173)</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you sign in with your Buksu student Google account, we receive from Google and store:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your <strong>student ID</strong> (the numeric part of your Buksu email address);</li>
        <li>your <strong>email address</strong> (for example <code>2401117078@student.buksu.edu.ph</code>);</li>
        <li>your <strong>display name</strong> and <strong>profile picture</strong>;</li>
        <li>the <strong>time of your first and most recent sign-in</strong>, and how many times you have signed in.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> receive or store your Google password, and we do not
        request access to your Gmail, Drive, Calendar, or any other Google data. The
        only thing we ask Google for is your basic identity
        (<code>openid email profile</code>).
      </p>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To admit you to the exams</strong> — confirming you are a Buksu student.</li>
        <li><strong>To keep your session open</strong> for up to 8 hours so you are not asked to sign in again mid-exam.</li>
        <li><strong>To let the instructor see who has used the practice exams</strong>, so support and class follow-up go to the right people.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
      <p>
        The record is stored in a <strong>Cloudflare D1</strong> database (Asia-Pacific
        region) owned by this project, and the sign-in exchange runs on a <strong>Cloudflare
        Worker</strong>. The site itself is static and hosted on GitHub Pages. Google acts
        as the identity provider and processes the sign-in under <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">Google's own privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your record is <strong>never sold, rented, or shared</strong> with advertisers
        or any third party. There is no tracking, no analytics, and no advertising on
        this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>We set two small cookies, both first-party and both required for signing in:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>ccna_session</code> — your signed-in session. It is <code>HttpOnly</code>,
          expires after 8 hours, and is deleted when you sign out.</li>
        <li><code>ccna_oauth_state</code> — a short-lived (10 minute) guard that protects
          the sign-in handshake against tampering. It is deleted as soon as the
          handshake finishes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We also store your exam progress, your settings, and your theme choice in your
        own browser so you can resume where you left off. Signed-out preview attempts
        stay on your device and are never sent to us — we only ever receive data after
        you sign in.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Records are kept while the course is running, and are deleted after the term
        ends or as soon as you ask — whichever comes first.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under RA 10173 you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>be told whether we hold a record about you, and to see a copy of it;</li>
        <li>have inaccurate information corrected;</li>
        <li>have your record erased;</li>
        <li>object to the processing of your record; and</li>
        <li>lodge a complaint with the <strong>National Privacy Commission</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these, email your instructor using the address you signed in
        with and ask for your record to be removed. There is no fee and no reason
        needed.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or your record: <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
      </p>

      <a class="policy-home" href={homeHref}>← Back to exam selection</a>
      <p class="policy-foot">
        This page is the privacy policy URL registered with our Google OAuth consent screen.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 44px 22px 80px;
  }

  .policy-kicker {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.9px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cyan);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .policy h1 {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-size: 30px;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
  }

  .policy-updated {
    margin: 0 0 26px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #8a8f94;
  }

  .policy h2 {
    margin: 30px 0 10px;
    font-size: 18px;
    letter-spacing: -0.2px;
  }

  .policy p,
  .policy li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .policy p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .policy ul {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }

  .policy li {
    margin-bottom: 7px;
  }

  .policy code {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    background: var(--cyan-soft);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 1px 6px;
  }

  .policy a {
    color: var(--cyan);
  }

  .policy-home {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 30px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .policy-home:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .policy-foot {
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: #8a8f94;
  }

  html[data-theme="dark"] .policy code {
    background: #2a3a40;
  }
</style>
